title Fold Q -- confer_one, and the absentees that dated the family
prompt Pick up the running thread Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, take the next agent-doable lap, send it.
think Standfast first. The ledger's rows 104 through 110 all carry closure notes, and the 20260821.042829 lap had already emptied the corrective queue by hand. Nothing open and agent-closable stands, so the constructive queue is honestly open.
think The running thread is the Caravan fold arc, and the last lap's recommend named confer_one the better crux of the three the queue printed -- forty rungs against provision_notes' twenty-four, and a family reaching table symbols fold O had already widened.
think Ran the carry scan live rather than trusting the printed queue in the log: provision_notes 2,093 across 24, confer_one 2,067 across 40, weigh_the_term 2,001 across 30. Chose confer_one on rung count, since a fold's reach across the ladder matters more than its line total.
think Fold O taught that a queue is a lead rather than a verdict, so hashed all forty-five bodies named confer_one before moving a line. Forty share one text at fifty-three lines, and 53 x 39 = 2,067 is exactly what the meter printed. Second lap running where the reading confirmed rather than corrected.
think Then the finding worth keeping. Diffed the five outliers against the canonical body and every one of them differs in exactly one place -- how deep it reaches into the report. Checked the ladder order from the imports rather than assuming it, and the five climb a staircase: confer 0, revoke 1, reclaim 2, abandon accessor+2, reckon accessor+3, and the forty above accessor+3 under a renamed accessor.
think Two things settle one rung apart. At abandon.rye the ladder stops counting inner hops and names the reach through below_of; at reckon.rye the depth settles at three; and from amend.rye up the accessor's name settles as abandoning_of. After those settlings the reach stops being a per-rung fact, which is precisely why the forty above are byte-identical and the five below cannot be.
think Widening survey came to 43 -- revoke_one private in all forty, abandoning_of private in three (appraise, bear, mend). Every other symbol the body reaches was already public. Added the entrust import to the harness after checking entrust.rye does not import ladder_checks back, so no cycle.
think Wrote in the README that the widenings split no family, then stopped and measured it rather than leaving the claim standing on the closing arithmetic. The measurement holds for a better reason than I had written: revoke_one stands in forty-four rungs as five families already, the folded forty sharing one body and the four elders each writing their own, so the whole family moved together; abandoning_of stands in forty rungs as forty distinct bodies carrying nothing, so widening three changed no membership. Corrected the sentence to say the measured truth.
think Council rota, lap index 1471 mod 27 = 13 -- foundations/20260702-165412_the-happy-zone-and-the-thin-edge.md. Its arithmetic is this arc's arithmetic: turn a multiplication into an addition, and earn by design the right to trust the sum. Forty rungs each carrying a body is the multiplication; one harness body behind a contract of one word is the addition, with each rung's delegate the collaboration side and its self-test the contract side.
obs Both arithmetics close with no remainder. The family gave back 2,067, the twelve-line delegate family carries 468, and the carry fell 1,599. On disk, independently, forty rungs shed forty-one lines apiece for 1,640, the harness took 100, and 368,641 is what wc reports.
obs The delegate is twelve lines here against fold P's three, because confer_one takes eight arguments where confer_slot takes two. A body's carry falls furthest when its signature is short and its interior is long, and this one is the opposite case -- fifty-three lines in, twelve back out.
obs A family's absentees are a reading in their own right. Fold P's two elders were an accident of ownership and one missing assert; fold Q's five are a dated sequence, and they name the two laps on which the ladder learned to name a reach instead of counting hops. That caution now stands in the scan's own header beside fold O's.
